      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The anterior deltoid is the prime shoulder flexor, alongside clavicular pectoralis major, and assists horizontal adduction and internal rotation. It contributes to abduction mainly above about 60 degrees and in the scapular plane. As the main resister of the shoulder-extension moment, it holds the upper arm still in curls and keeps the arm overhead in triceps extensions, so it is the primary shoulder_position_hold muscle.",
      "status": "reviewed"
